[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and marked known, with one fix queued for the
parser. Read report by report, it holds more than one problem, and the queued fix covers only the
first. Each problem now has a ticket of its own.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## The problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** A day-first tenant writes 7/4 for
7 April and gets an invite for 4 July. It reaches every tenant through every channel. This is the
problem #4471 describes, and the queued fix is for it.

**`hint`: booking-v3's form tells people to type the month first.** It prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under
its date field, people type what it says, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first.
The symptom is the same swap, so the reports read like the parser's. The code is different: fixing
the parser leaves it as it is. It only comes through the form, only for tenants on booking-v3.

**`one-day`: a date moves by one day.** "Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May." "Client in
Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday. Same meeting." A month-first parser swaps day and
month; it cannot move a date by one day. A time zone applied at a day boundary can. The desk noticed
these (`desk-notes.json`) and keeps them counted under the parser by tenant. They stay counted there,
and have a ticket of their own.

<Callout kind="warn">
When the parser fix ships, #4471 will look closed. The form hint and the one-day move stay open,
and their reports keep arriving with the same subject lines.
</Callout>

## Why one ticket held them all

- The desk merges on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). All of
  these problems produce the same subjects, "Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong", so subject
  matching cannot keep them apart.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, not the tenant's locale and form. The note
  under the table shows how often it names the wrong problem.
- The ticket export pages overlap, so the same report can come twice. Count by report id.

## For the desk

- Keep #4471 for the parser. Move the `hint` and `one-day` reports to their own tickets, linked in
  the table.
- Decision 0001 stays as written. A new record should replace it: merge on cause (tenant, channel,
  booking form), checked against the report's words, not on subject.

